+/**
+ * Whether a rule from an unkeyed chain is offered to this node
+ * (VitaSurf).
+ *
+ * The tests only ever answer together, so their order is free, and it
+ * is cheapest first: what the entry itself holds -- the state and
+ * attributes the key compound needs and the ancestor bloom -- before
+ * the sheet list, and only then the reads through the selector into
+ * its rule, which on the Vita are a cache miss each. On a saved GitHub
+ * page the universal chain was walked 447,601 times to offer 60,492
+ * rules, and most of the rest fail on the bloom.
+ */
+#define ENTRY_OFFERED(e, req) \
